14.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {I agree with the overwhelming consensus around H.384 as the cleanest one-round, six-hit Counterstrike expectation under the conventional creature-first stance convention (D* ≈ 20.5) and standard 5 % linearisation with the 20–50 Archangel band. That framing keeps Protection from Water and the listed secondaries as pure distractors while respecting speed-9 timing and Basic Defense applying only to incoming damage.

Colleague 1’s stance-ordering observation is a fair point to examine, but switching the multiplier after the hero defense addition produces an inconsistent result with the H3/HotA worksheet implementations that most of us are referencing. The same holds for any attempt to widen the damage band via Expert Ballistics; that skill does not alter Archangel melee output here. The minor Expert Earth Magic terrain/Stone Skin overlap Col1 flags can introduce a +1 Δ adjustment on the opening exchange under that alternative ordering, which would land a near-miss total right around 397, yet it still rests on a non-standard bookkeeping step that the group has already set aside in favor of the creature-first convention. Once that convention is locked in, the arithmetic remains firmly at 384 without needing further tweaks.

If we can confirm the stance convention first, the remaining variants (412, 439, etc.) drop away cleanly.}

